sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
Grid items can occupy more than one column. `grid-column: 1 / -1` tells an item to start at the first Grid line and end at the last one, creating a full-width row when that layout is useful.

**Worked example:**

```css
main > :first-child {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
}
```

**Line by line:** `main > :first-child {` selects only the first direct child inside the existing `main` Grid. `grid-column: 1 / -1;` places that item from the first column line through the final column line. The closing `}` ends the rule.

